@lrf=1|aud=LLM|scope=continue
R|continue.scope|task:continue|MUST|RO_LOCAL|subject=PADDOCK CONTINUE/1 execution; apply this user instruction only to issue resolution performed while continuing this PADDOCK repository; do not apply to another repository, an unrelated task, or a non-CONTINUE execution
R|continue.issue.memory|task:continue|MUST|LIVE_WRITE|when a PADDOCK Issue reaches [x] after its acceptance checks, Runner evidence, separate review, and Main reconciliation, ingest only verified non-secret issue outcome and receipt evidence into llm-mem category knowledge; report the actual ingest result/reference; if the executable is unavailable or ingest fails, stop before selecting another Issue and report failure; never ingest credentials, raw URLs, or unverified claims
R|continue.issue.push|task:continue|MUST|VCS_WRITE|after that Issue reaches [x] and its verified outcome is successfully ingested to llm-mem, determine the exact issue-scoped files and upstream-to-HEAD commit range; present include/exclude paths, commits, and target upstream to the user and obtain explicit current-task approval before any staging, commit, or push; after approval, stage and commit only the independently verified Issue changes and necessary Issue/receipt/generated-index updates, then push to the current branch's already configured upstream; verify every commit in the push range belongs only to the approved Issue batch; preserve unrelated dirty/untracked work; do not force-push, rewrite history, change remotes, or claim success unless the command succeeds; if exact isolation/upstream cannot be verified or push fails, preserve local state, report and stop before the next Issue
R|continue.issue.dependency-closure|task:continue|MAY|RO_LOCAL|if an issue-scoped push is blocked solely by required untracked/uncommitted source/build dependencies, Main may continue only the minimal dependency Issue closure established by a read-only Git/status/import/build-scope audit; record exact dependency Issue IDs and file edges in Cursor before CODE; every dependency retains its own state, acceptance, verification and effect gates and receives its own verified llm-mem ingest at [x]; do not start unrelated Issues or stage/commit/push unresolved or unverified dependency work; after the closure is verified, present one exact grouped include/exclude and upstream commit range for explicit current-task approval before any VCS write; uncertainty=STOP+ask
R|continue.issue.not-global|task:continue|MUST_NOT|VCS_WRITE|this instruction does not apply outside PADDOCK CONTINUE/1 and does not permit staging, committing, or pushing unrelated repository changes, another repository, or unverified Issue work
